WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.445 --> 00:00:01.818
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.818 --> 00:00:05.055
Today's message is Ignore the Little Man.

00:00:05.055 --> 00:00:07.071
Over to you, Kate Winslet.

00:00:07.071 --> 00:00:09.089
(rooster crows)

00:00:09.089 --> 00:00:11.647
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.647 --> 00:00:14.306
♫ Ent-spresso keep me going

00:00:14.306 --> 00:00:18.545
♫ I wake up every morning ♫

00:00:18.545 --> 00:00:21.521
- When I was younger, when I was only 14,

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.781
I was told by a drama teacher

00:00:23.781 --> 00:00:26.375
that I might do okay if
I was happy to settle

00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:28.292
for the fat girl parts.

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:30.449
Look at me now.

00:00:31.391 --> 00:00:32.711
Look at me now.

00:00:32.711 --> 00:00:35.905
So, what I feel like saying
in those moments is to,

00:00:35.905 --> 00:00:39.020
you know, any young woman
who has ever been put down

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.421
by a teacher or a friend or even a parent,

00:00:42.421 --> 00:00:44.780
just don't listen to any of it,

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:46.492
because that's what I did.

00:00:46.492 --> 00:00:49.277
I didn't listen, and I kept on going,

00:00:49.277 --> 00:00:51.857
and I overcame all of
my fears and I got over

00:00:51.857 --> 00:00:55.313
a lot of insecurity,
and just keep doing it,

00:00:55.313 --> 00:00:57.068
and keep believing in yourself, you know?

00:00:57.068 --> 00:01:00.250
That's what I felt like I
really had to dig deep and do,

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:04.017
and so I would dedicate
it to all those you women

00:01:04.017 --> 00:01:07.036
who doubt themselves, because
you shouldn't be doubting.

00:01:07.036 --> 00:01:09.003
You should just be going for it.

00:01:09.003 --> 00:01:11.057
- If you're trying to do
something big and important,

00:01:11.057 --> 00:01:13.195
then you're going to have
people who are going to try

00:01:13.195 --> 00:01:14.156
to tear you down.

00:01:14.156 --> 00:01:14.989
It's going to happen.

00:01:14.989 --> 00:01:16.405
If you stand for something important,

00:01:16.405 --> 00:01:18.999
if you have a big mission that
you're trying to accomplish,

00:01:18.999 --> 00:01:21.084
then you're going to have
people who you stand against.

00:01:21.084 --> 00:01:24.089
You're going to have
people who are in your way,

00:01:24.089 --> 00:01:28.256
even if you have the most
noble, positive mission.

00:01:29.105 --> 00:01:31.272
You look at mine, Believe.

00:01:32.404 --> 00:01:35.182
Right? Like how do you hate on Believe?

00:01:35.182 --> 00:01:38.900
How do you hate on believing
in people to do amazing things?

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:41.918
There's no negativity in my message.

00:01:41.918 --> 00:01:44.660
I'm not making videos
about how people suck.

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:47.333
It's intentional to make
everything positive,

00:01:47.333 --> 00:01:49.500
and, honestly, to the
detriment of my channel.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.010
Like I could get way more views
and subscribers and comments

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:55.095
if I was antagonizing people

00:01:55.095 --> 00:01:56.548
and telling people that they suck.

00:01:56.548 --> 00:01:58.858
I don't want to build
that kind of channel.

00:01:58.858 --> 00:02:00.839
I don't want to have that kind of vision

00:02:00.839 --> 00:02:01.672
for what I'm building,

00:02:01.672 --> 00:02:03.241
but even then, even though we're staying

00:02:03.241 --> 00:02:04.711
on the positive always,

00:02:04.711 --> 00:02:06.933
we get people who hate the message.

00:02:06.933 --> 00:02:10.459
We get the little man,
who is going to hate

00:02:10.459 --> 00:02:11.854
and attack people,

00:02:11.854 --> 00:02:14.174
and say that what they're doing is stupid,

00:02:14.174 --> 00:02:18.096
and so, no matter how big or how positive

00:02:18.096 --> 00:02:19.796
a thing is that you have to do,

00:02:19.796 --> 00:02:21.643
that this is what you're
taking a stance on,

00:02:21.643 --> 00:02:23.225
you're going to have people
who just don't like it,

00:02:23.225 --> 00:02:25.089
and it's their issue more than you.

00:02:25.089 --> 00:02:26.955
They had something in their past that

00:02:26.955 --> 00:02:29.682
is coming up, and they don't
want to see you be successful.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.273
It has nothing to do with you.

00:02:31.273 --> 00:02:33.005
It's all them and their issue.

00:02:33.005 --> 00:02:36.755
See, I see entrepreneurs
as heroes, you know?

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:40.307
I see entrepreneurs,

00:02:42.123 --> 00:02:45.411
we're about to take our at-bat, right?

00:02:45.411 --> 00:02:46.674
We're in the stadium.

00:02:46.674 --> 00:02:48.103
We've been practicing.

00:02:48.103 --> 00:02:50.148
We've been working to
get to the major leagues.

00:02:50.148 --> 00:02:52.067
We've been grinding and hustling,

00:02:52.067 --> 00:02:53.987
and this is our chance, right?

00:02:53.987 --> 00:02:55.810
This is our chance to do something,

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:58.404
and 70% of at-bats in baseball,

00:02:58.404 --> 00:03:01.415
70% of at-bats are out, for a good hitter,

00:03:01.415 --> 00:03:03.451
for the best hitters in the world.

00:03:03.451 --> 00:03:06.823
They will only get a hit 30% of the time.

00:03:06.823 --> 00:03:08.796
That happens to entrepreneurs, too.

00:03:08.796 --> 00:03:11.926
Most of the things that
we try aren't amazing.

00:03:11.926 --> 00:03:14.324
Most of the things that we try don't work.

00:03:14.324 --> 00:03:17.080
I've thrown away, I've
tried and thrown away

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:20.073
more ideas than most people even start,

00:03:20.073 --> 00:03:21.664
so expect to get out a lot.

00:03:21.664 --> 00:03:23.474
Expect to get a lot of failure, right?

00:03:23.474 --> 00:03:24.610
But finally, we've made it.

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:26.091
We've got our big at-bat.

00:03:26.091 --> 00:03:27.094
This is it, right?

00:03:27.094 --> 00:03:28.039
Maybe we'll get a single.

00:03:28.039 --> 00:03:29.575
Maybe we just get to first base.

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:32.224
Maybe we get a little bit of contact.

00:03:32.224 --> 00:03:34.253
We get to second base, we get a double,

00:03:34.253 --> 00:03:37.462
and maybe, maybe this idea
that you have right now,

00:03:37.462 --> 00:03:39.300
maybe this amazing
thing that's inside you,

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.864
maybe the timing is just right.

00:03:40.864 --> 00:03:43.002
Maybe the execution is just right,

00:03:43.002 --> 00:03:45.016
and you see that pitch counting down.

00:03:45.016 --> 00:03:46.240
This is your moment.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.007
All that hard work, all that practice.

00:03:48.007 --> 00:03:49.979
This is your time.

00:03:49.979 --> 00:03:51.132
Right?

00:03:51.132 --> 00:03:53.536
And you smash the home run.

00:03:53.536 --> 00:03:54.934
That's what we want.

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.909
That's what we've been
working so hard for.

00:03:56.909 --> 00:03:59.211
That's what we put up
with all the failure for,

00:03:59.211 --> 00:04:02.356
to hit that home run,
to run around the bases,

00:04:02.356 --> 00:04:05.815
to celebrate, to do something
meaningful and impactful.

00:04:05.815 --> 00:04:07.401
Who's the little man?

00:04:07.401 --> 00:04:10.102
The little man is the
guy just watching you.

00:04:10.102 --> 00:04:12.214
The little man is the
guy up in the stands,

00:04:12.214 --> 00:04:15.382
buying his Crackerjacks, buying some beer,

00:04:15.382 --> 00:04:17.222
and yelling insults at you,

00:04:17.222 --> 00:04:18.740
and telling you that you suck,

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:20.431
and telling you all the reasons why

00:04:20.431 --> 00:04:22.037
you're never going to hit a home run,

00:04:22.037 --> 00:04:24.035
throwing popcorn down at you,

00:04:24.035 --> 00:04:26.581
saying go home, go home, you bum.

00:04:26.581 --> 00:04:28.563
That's what the little man is,

00:04:28.563 --> 00:04:31.254
the people who are too afraid to get up

00:04:31.254 --> 00:04:33.005
and go do something themselves,

00:04:33.005 --> 00:04:35.311
the people who are too
afraid to put in the work

00:04:35.311 --> 00:04:36.739
to get their at-bat.

00:04:36.739 --> 00:04:38.891
They're going to bring on
everybody else around them,

00:04:38.891 --> 00:04:41.064
and maybe they took an at-bat once.

00:04:41.064 --> 00:04:42.813
Maybe they took their shot.

00:04:42.813 --> 00:04:44.803
Maybe they tried to
believe in themselves once.

00:04:44.803 --> 00:04:45.800
Maybe they had that idea

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.558
and they tried to do something with it,

00:04:47.558 --> 00:04:50.014
and they failed, and it didn't work out,

00:04:50.014 --> 00:04:52.502
and the story they tell themselves now is

00:04:52.502 --> 00:04:55.089
it's never going to work.

00:04:55.089 --> 00:04:57.366
And of course, it can't
be their fault, right?

00:04:57.366 --> 00:04:58.710
It's not their fault.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:01.305
It's somebody else's fault,
the economy, the government,

00:05:01.305 --> 00:05:05.332
the president, schooling,
lack of resources,

00:05:05.332 --> 00:05:06.856
lack of money, whatever it is.

00:05:06.856 --> 00:05:07.981
It's always somebody else's fault,

00:05:07.981 --> 00:05:09.735
and because they didn't have success,

00:05:09.735 --> 00:05:11.930
now you can't either.

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:13.913
Look at the people in
your life who are hating

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:15.978
on your idea, really
hating, like the little man,

00:05:15.978 --> 00:05:18.690
the people telling you
that you can never do this,

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:20.825
the people who are
really stomping you down.

00:05:20.825 --> 00:05:24.242
Have they done what you are trying to do?

00:05:25.696 --> 00:05:27.275
Whatever your mission is,

00:05:27.275 --> 00:05:28.385
whatever your ambition is,

00:05:28.385 --> 00:05:31.278
have they done what you are trying to do?

00:05:31.278 --> 00:05:34.239
Have they hit the ball
like you want to hit it?

00:05:34.239 --> 00:05:36.672
Have they hit their
home run in the same way

00:05:36.672 --> 00:05:37.752
you want to hit yours?

00:05:37.752 --> 00:05:39.618
Have they done it?

00:05:39.618 --> 00:05:43.497
(inspirational guitar music)

00:05:43.497 --> 00:05:45.624
Stop listening to them.

00:05:45.624 --> 00:05:47.529
They are cancer.

00:05:47.529 --> 00:05:49.792
The more you spend around those people,

00:05:49.792 --> 00:05:52.549
the more you believe what they believe,

00:05:52.549 --> 00:05:54.978
the more you become one of them,

00:05:54.978 --> 00:05:57.510
the more that big idea that you have

00:05:57.510 --> 00:05:59.872
gets further and further from reality,

00:05:59.872 --> 00:06:02.340
and you start thinking oh,
that was really stupid,

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:03.574
and you become like them,

00:06:03.574 --> 00:06:06.086
and then you start dragging
other people down as well.

00:06:06.086 --> 00:06:07.072
Don't do that.

00:06:07.072 --> 00:06:08.786
Don't pay attention to the little man.

00:06:08.786 --> 00:06:10.584
Create a better environment.

00:06:10.584 --> 00:06:11.846
Change your friends.

00:06:11.846 --> 00:06:13.492
Change your resources you consume.

00:06:13.492 --> 00:06:15.522
Change the videos that you watch.

00:06:15.522 --> 00:06:18.166
Create a morning routine
and a ritual and a habit

00:06:18.166 --> 00:06:21.583
that sets you up for boldness, every day,

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:25.221
'cause you got to put in the work

00:06:25.221 --> 00:06:26.792
to get your at-bat.

00:06:26.792 --> 00:06:28.971
You got to put in the work,

00:06:28.971 --> 00:06:30.196
and even when you get there,

00:06:30.196 --> 00:06:33.085
to the major leagues,
you're going to get out

00:06:33.085 --> 00:06:34.835
70% of the time.

00:06:35.709 --> 00:06:37.586
Doesn't matter.

00:06:37.586 --> 00:06:39.165
Doesn't matter that you failed.

00:06:39.165 --> 00:06:41.030
Doesn't matter that the
fans are booing at you.

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:44.251
Doesn't matter they're
throwing peanuts at you.

00:06:44.251 --> 00:06:46.584
You want to hit that home run?

00:06:48.904 --> 00:06:49.987
You're ready.

00:06:50.932 --> 00:06:52.331
Believe.

00:06:52.331 --> 00:06:54.481
So the question today is: I'm curious,

00:06:54.481 --> 00:06:57.707
who has been the little man in your life?

00:06:57.707 --> 00:06:59.117
Leave it in the comments below.

00:06:59.117 --> 00:07:00.120
I'm curious to find out.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:02.808
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Katrina Megginson.

00:07:02.808 --> 00:07:04.548
Thank you so much, Katrina,
for picking up a copy

00:07:04.548 --> 00:07:06.002
of my book, Your One Word.

00:07:06.002 --> 00:07:07.992
Really, really, really means a lot to me,

00:07:07.992 --> 00:07:09.403
and I hope you're enjoying the read,

00:07:09.403 --> 00:07:11.146
so thank you guys again for watching.

00:07:11.146 --> 00:07:12.075
I believe in you.

00:07:12.075 --> 00:07:14.076
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:07:14.076 --> 00:07:17.012
and whatever your one word is, much love,

00:07:17.012 --> 00:07:18.494
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:07:18.494 --> 00:07:21.536
for another shot of Ent-spresso.

00:07:21.536 --> 00:07:23.814
♫ I wake up every morning

00:07:23.814 --> 00:07:27.847
♫ Ent-spresso keep me going ♫

00:07:27.847 --> 00:07:31.180
(typewriter clatters)

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:33.662
♫ I keep on falling

00:07:33.662 --> 00:07:35.707
♫ In and out

00:07:35.707 --> 00:07:38.642
♫ Of love with you

00:07:38.642 --> 00:07:41.163
♫ I never

00:07:41.163 --> 00:07:43.015
♫ Loved someone

00:07:43.015 --> 00:07:46.881
♫ Way that I love you

00:07:46.881 --> 00:07:48.626
♫ Oh baby ♫

00:07:48.626 --> 00:07:50.107
When I sing that song, every night,

00:07:50.107 --> 00:07:53.822
I'm like wow, like who'd have thought

00:07:53.822 --> 00:07:56.458
that all of this from
that, you know what I mean?

00:07:56.458 --> 00:07:58.801
And you know, people told us that was

00:07:58.801 --> 00:08:00.103
a bad record to go with.

00:08:00.103 --> 00:08:02.724
Nobody plays, you know, slow records.

00:08:02.724 --> 00:08:03.888
It'll never cross over.

00:08:03.888 --> 00:08:05.001
Nobody's going to get it.

00:08:05.001 --> 00:08:06.155
You won't make it, dah dah dah.

00:08:06.155 --> 00:08:08.030
I mean, they told us
everything under the sun,

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:10.212
but it felt good and it felt special,

00:08:10.212 --> 00:08:12.418
and when people heard it, they were moved,

00:08:12.418 --> 00:08:15.232
and you know, all the
pieces just fell into place,

00:08:15.232 --> 00:08:18.166
so it's definitely, you
know, my calling card.

00:08:18.166 --> 00:08:20.263
It's like my little baby, you know?

00:08:20.263 --> 00:08:22.774
And I cherish and respect it.

00:08:22.774 --> 00:08:25.408
- Yeah, don't let cool people
tell you you're not cool,

00:08:25.408 --> 00:08:27.284
'cause they're not cool,

00:08:27.284 --> 00:08:29.961
so, you know, I was a loser for, you know,

00:08:29.961 --> 00:08:32.378
by stereotype for many years,

00:08:33.539 --> 00:08:37.711
and it's like the classic
case of look at me now,

00:08:37.711 --> 00:08:38.896
you know what I mean?

00:08:38.896 --> 00:08:40.573
So, I mean, let me tell you something,

00:08:40.573 --> 00:08:41.853
if you're out there right now,

00:08:41.853 --> 00:08:44.239
and you like have no idea who you are

00:08:44.239 --> 00:08:46.013
or what you belong to,

00:08:46.013 --> 00:08:46.930
it took me,

00:08:48.335 --> 00:08:49.188
I don't know, man.

00:08:49.188 --> 00:08:51.078
I just figured out last year.

00:08:51.078 --> 00:08:52.480
Last year was the first time I ever like

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:55.852
looked in the mirror and
was like I like that guy.

00:08:55.852 --> 00:08:57.519
It took me 25 years,

00:08:59.411 --> 00:09:00.494
and you know,

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:02.949
I don't know.

00:09:02.949 --> 00:09:05.171
Don't listen, don't listen to
what the cool people say, man.

00:09:05.171 --> 00:09:06.004
They're not cool.

00:09:06.004 --> 00:09:06.837
Do what you do.

00:09:06.837 --> 00:09:07.906
What you do is cool.

00:09:07.906 --> 00:09:10.748
- Ignore people telling
you your idea is bad.

00:09:10.748 --> 00:09:12.723
They may be right, but
the only way to know

00:09:12.723 --> 00:09:14.415
is to actually build it out,

00:09:14.415 --> 00:09:18.423
and I think the thing that
works about Silicon Valley

00:09:18.423 --> 00:09:19.928
that's different than Mexico City

00:09:19.928 --> 00:09:21.887
or almost anywhere else in the world

00:09:21.887 --> 00:09:25.069
is the default response,
if someone says hey,

00:09:25.069 --> 00:09:27.043
I'm going to start a
startup, here's my idea,

00:09:27.043 --> 00:09:29.226
the default response is to be excited,

00:09:29.226 --> 00:09:32.160
and think like, oh, why might that work?

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:34.120
And in most of the rest of the world,

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:36.275
the default response, when
you tell someone your idea,

00:09:36.275 --> 00:09:38.643
is to say oh, that's not going to work,

00:09:38.643 --> 00:09:41.075
and this is really toxic for startups,

00:09:41.075 --> 00:09:43.269
'cause you have to believe in yourself,

00:09:43.269 --> 00:09:46.240
and the good ideas, because
they sound like bad ideas,

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:49.491
are so fragile and so killable,

00:09:49.491 --> 00:09:51.388
that you have to be really careful

00:09:51.388 --> 00:09:52.987
to insulate yourself against this.

